This product includes no third-party code. Every script is Python
standard library only.

It generates configuration that downloads and runs the following
third-party tools, each under its own licence:

  DITA Open Toolkit          Apache-2.0    https://www.dita-ot.org/
  Vale                       MIT           https://vale.sh/
  Prettier + plugin-xml      MIT           https://prettier.io/
  husky, lint-staged         MIT
  SchXslt                    MIT           https://codeberg.org/SchXslt/schxslt
  jing                       BSD           https://relaxng.org/jclark/jing.html

The idea that DITA belongs in a docs-as-code model is not ours. It was
argued publicly by Tech Writer Koduje (https://techwriterkoduje.pl/dita-as-code/)
and pioneered by DITA For Small Teams (http://www.d4st.org/).
